From: Lorenzo Giannoccaro <giannoccarol@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:54:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: aidl: optionally write the firmware path for every chip
 mode

The firmware path is written only for the V1 STA and AP modes. A
built-in qcacld driver unloads itself when every interface goes down
and loads again only on a firmware path write, so with a V3 or dynamic
chip mode Wi-Fi stayed off after it had been turned off once. With
ro.vendor.wifi.fw_path_any_mode set, write the STA firmware path for
the other modes too; the write is a no-op when the driver is loaded.

Change-Id: Ia5ba3dbd2daf7a91bb23ba81fc0301904329c22f
---
 wifi/aidl/default/wifi_chip.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_chip.cpp b/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_chip.cpp
index 7df168e..bd299b8 100644
--- a/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_chip.cpp
+++ b/wifi/aidl/default/wifi_chip.cpp
@@ -1453,6 +1453,11 @@ ndk::ScopedAStatus WifiChip::handleChipConfiguration(
         success = mode_controller_.lock()->changeFirmwareMode(IfaceType::STA);
     } else if (mode_id == feature_flags::chip_mode_ids::kV1Ap) {
         success = mode_controller_.lock()->changeFirmwareMode(IfaceType::AP);
+    } else if (property_get_bool("ro.vendor.wifi.fw_path_any_mode", false)) {
+        // Built-in drivers that unload themselves when every interface is
+        // down (qcacld "enter low power") are loaded again by a firmware path
+        // write; do it for the dynamic/V3 modes too, not only for V1.
+        success = mode_controller_.lock()->changeFirmwareMode(IfaceType::STA);
     }
     if (!success) {
         return createWifiStatus(WifiStatusCode::ERROR_UNKNOWN);
